=2 Walkthrough
!The Eldieme Necropolis-map1.jpg|right|Necropolis Map 1
!The Eldieme Necropolis-map2.jpg|right|Necropolis Map 2
\**{c=red:Note:}** To get a {i:Purple Ribbon|Purple Ribbon|13569}, you must first talk to {n:Roberta} in {z:Windurst Woods} (I-13) inside the **Nchaa's Good Goods** shop.
* Give the {i:Purple Ribbon|Purple Ribbon|13569} to {n:Kerutoto} (J-8) {z:Windurst Waters South|Windurst Waters} (northern **Rhinostery** building).
** You will receive 3,600 gil.
** You must wait one Earth minute before you talk to Kerutoto again, she will give you back the item. If you are eligible to take on the quest {q:Waking Dreams|Waking Dreams|Waking Dreams} you must accept the option to fight Diabolos before her dialogue will move on.
* Go to The {z:Eldieme Necropolis} from the (J-10) entrance in {z:Batallia Downs}. If you have unlocked it before, the {p:Survival Guide} teleport will take you there.
** You will need a {@k} {k:Magicked astrolabe} or a friend to help hit switches to open doors.

=3 Navigating The Eldieme Necropolis
* Upon entering, go straight until you come to an intersection at (J-8) and take a left.
* Follow the path west until you reach **Titan's Gate** at (G-8).
* Go north through **Titan's Gate** and step on the square of bones, you will fall below and reach Map 2 (L-10).
* After the fall, go east to the **Hume Bones** at (M-10).
* Trade the {i:Purple Ribbon|Purple Ribbon|13569} to **Hume Bones** at (M-10), which will spawn {m:Lich C Magnus}.
** Note that Lich C Magnus has a chance to drop the unique Lvl. 50 Club {p:Lilith's Rod} with an MP Drain effect.
** If the rod doesn't drop, rezone without touching the **Hume Bones** and repeat the quest from beginning for another chance.
** If you lose the {i:Purple Ribbon|Purple Ribbon|13569}, you must wait until next {p:Conquest Tally} to get it back.
** If multiple party members need this quest, you must wait 5 minutes after defeat between each spawn.
* Check the **Hume Bones** again after NM is defeated to receive {i:Blue Ribbon|Blue Ribbon|12521}.

You can return to {n:Kerutoto} and complete the quest.
